$667
{"role": "assistant", "content": "The pragmatic playbook lists the following principles:\n\n- **SLOs lead decision\u2011making** \u2013 fidelity choices (e.g., quantization, model variant, batching) must be selected to meet the agreed\u2011upon SLO window, not the other way around.  \n- **Measure before change** \u2013 gather at least 7\u202fdays of representative telemetry before finalizing the fidelity package.  \n- **Guardrails** \u2013 automated quality checks (using sample prompts) must pass before any lower\u2011cost fidelity modes are enabled.  \n\nThese principles are outlined in the playbook\u2019s \u201cPrinciples\u201d section\u3010chunk-6\u3011."}
