$1556
{"role": "assistant", "content": "The document is a **pragmatic playbook for onboarding customers onto SLO\u2011driven fidelity tiers**. It explains how to map customer SLOs (latency, availability, correctness) to recommended fidelity tiers, what telemetry is required, what operational checks are needed, and provides a step\u2011by\u2011step checklist for both commercial and technical leads. It is intended for use when contracting customers for dedicated or private deployments and when migrating high\u2011usage tenants from hosted to dedicated environments\u3010chunk-2\u3011.  \n\n**Legal / Commercial alignment step** (the first item in the operational checklist) requires:  \n\n- Confirming the target SLOs, the billing model (usage vs. reserved), and the trial period.  \n- Documenting these commitments in a CD/contract appendix, including fallback and rollback terms\u3010chunk-12\u3011.  \n\n**Intended audience**  \n\n- Product managers and solutions engineering  \n- Customer success and account teams  \n- Platform and runtime engineers (serving, routing, telemetry)\u3010chunk-4\u3011.  \n\n**Ownership / contact fields** \u2013 The supplied chunks list the stakeholder groups but do not provide specific ownership or contact fields for each group.  \n\n**Related operational checklist sections** \u2013 The document includes a numbered operational checklist; the first section is the legal/commercial alignment step described above. Additional checklist items are implied but not detailed in the provided excerpts\u3010chunk-12\u3011.  "}
